course: dictionary
lesson: 10058
title: Testosterone: a hormone for growing up
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A hormone is a chemical messenger in your body. It travels in your blood and tells other parts of your body what to do. Testosterone is one of these messengers.
explain: Men and boys have much more testosterone than women and girls, but everyone has some. It helps the body grow muscles and bones.
explain: During puberty, the years when a child's body starts to become an adult's, testosterone helps cause changes such as a deeper voice and facial hair in boys. «Bigger differences in strength and speed appear in the teens, when boys make much more testosterone.»
fact: A hormone is a chemical messenger in the body.
fact: Testosterone is a hormone. Men and boys have much more of it, but women and girls have some too.
fact: Testosterone helps the body grow muscles and bones.
fact: During puberty, testosterone can cause a deeper voice and facial hair in boys.
fact: Testosterone does not decide everything. People's behaviour depends on many things, and everyone is responsible for their own choices.
exercise: What is a hormone? | A school subject | A kind of muscle | *A chemical messenger in the body | A type of bone
exercise: «Bigger differences in strength and speed appear in the teens, when boys make much more testosterone.» Which group has much more testosterone? | Everyone equally | Babies only | *Men and boys | Women and girls
exercise: What does testosterone help the body do? | *Grow muscles and bones | Turn hair blue | Stop the body from growing | Make food into light
test: During puberty, what change can testosterone help cause in boys? | A change in the time of sunrise | Hair that grows on the tongue | Eyes that glow in the dark | *A deeper voice
test: Who has some testosterone in their body? | *Women, girls, men and boys | Only boys in their teens | Nobody at all | Only men
exam: Which statement about testosterone is true? | Nobody has any of it at all | *Men and boys have much more of it than women and girls, but everyone has some | Only boys have it, and only during the teenage years | Women have much more of it than men
